* ZSHOW - INSPECT THE Z-SYSTEM

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* ZSHOW - INSPECT THE Z-SYSTEM

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:ZSHOW [menu-choice]

Displays the Z-System environment, installed packages and configuration.
With no selection, presents its information menu. This is the ZSHOW
filename even though the internal banner may say SHOW.

Some options such as /E install or change an error handler; treat those as
configuration changes. DRI SHOW is a separate CP/M 3 status utility. Do
not publish environment dumps containing private directory information.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
